# oc-sync settings. Copy to .env and fill in — .env is gitignored, this file is not.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The repo is public: host names, addresses and usernames belong here, never in
# bin/oc-sync or any tracked file. Prefer ssh-config aliases over raw addresses
# (measured ~11.4s per ssh call by raw IP versus ~1.4s by alias on this network).

# Whitespace, comma or newline separated. One entry per line is clearest.
OC_HOSTS="host-a host-b"

# Optional overrides. The defaults are shown; you only need these if your layout
# differs from a standard one.
# OC_HOSTS_FILE="$HOME/.oc-hosts"    # legacy fallback, used when OC_HOSTS is unset
# OC_SCRIPT="bin/oc"                 # the helper pushed to each host's ~/bin
# OC_SYNC_CONFIG_DIR="."             # root of the opencode config pushed by --with-config
# OC_SYNC_ENV_FILE=".env"            # this file
# OC_LOCAL_USER=""                   # defaults to $(whoami) on this machine
# OC_SYNC_SSH_TIMEOUT=90             # per remote command
# OC_SYNC_RSYNC_TIMEOUT=120          # per transfer